to love who they love?

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:47.110
- Oh, maybe I should just
break out in some gospel songs,

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.250
screamin' and hollerin' and hootin'.

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:50.803
Oh Lordy, Lordy!

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.210
- No, this isn't the speech yet.

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:55.000
Can I just do the speech?

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:58.110
- Oh, you want this bitch
to shut up, is that it?

00:13:58.110 --> 00:13:59.360
- What's the matter, the Black guy's

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:02.050
making way too much noise in
your movie theater, massa?

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:05.220
- Forgive me for lisping and
lilting through your speech.

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:06.226
- No, I just meant-

00:14:06.226 --> 00:14:07.679
- Whoa! (in unison)

00:14:07.679 --> 00:14:10.420
- What's with the hands
man, I ain't gonna shoot ya!

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:12.110
- What are you going
to grab my breasts now?

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:14.990
- Protect yourself from the gay invasion.

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:15.908
- Guys!

00:14:15.908 --> 00:14:17.580
- Oh, guys!

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:18.620
Should I leave?

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:20.080
Sorry, men and women.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.110
- Let's exclude everybody

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.520
who identifies themselves
as something else

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:23.620
because they're not people!

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:24.730
- I meant people!

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.600
- Whose people?

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:26.710
My people?

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.520
Do I speak for my people?

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:29.530
- All right!

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:30.760
- More like all white!

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.700
- More like no rights!

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:35.990
- More like women are
second-class citizens, right?

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:37.430
- 'Kay, stop!

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.870
Men, women, people of
all ethnicities, genders,

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:43.130
sexual orientation, religion.

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:45.823
Can I please just get to my speech?

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:48.603
- Fine.

00:14:48.603 --> 00:14:49.452
- Yeah.

00:14:49.452 --> 00:14:51.093
- Mm-hmm.

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.223
- Okay, here goes.

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:58.430
A Chinaman, a Polak and
an Arab walk into a bar.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:14:59.290
- I love Arab jokes.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.950
- Ching chong, bring it on.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.453
- You had me at Polak.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:07.690
- Noah Sanders, I'm here
for the job interview.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:10.068
- Please take a seat, Mr.
Weinstein will see you next.

00:15:10.068 --> 00:15:12.735
(calming music)

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:25.733
- Job interviews, huh?

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.321
Never fun.

00:15:28.321 --> 00:15:30.760
(man sighs)

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.350
Okay.

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:33.723
I get it, stay focused.

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:37.357
Cool, cool, cool cool...

00:15:39.992 --> 00:15:43.420
(men laughing behind door)

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:44.253
Ooh.

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:48.093
That's a big laugh.

00:15:50.675 --> 00:15:52.511
(sighs)

00:15:52.511 --> 00:15:54.100
- [Mr. Weinstein] Oh no!
- [Adam] I did it!

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.656
- [Mr. Weinstein] No you didn't!

00:15:55.656 --> 00:15:58.410
(men laughing behind door)

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:03.410
